	(text "Notes:\n1) Reverse-engineered from the physical board. Not a manufacturer drawing. \n   Signal names from the DSI manual are used where they existl all others, and\n   all symbol references are the author's.  Symbol reference physical locations \n   documented separately.\n2) U27 outputs are decoded codes 1-4; their meanings are:\n  1) Reader on\n  2) Punch on\n  3) Reader off\n  4) Punch Off\n3) Inter-sheet connections are carried by global labels. Lines between sheet\n   blocks on this sheet are illustrative only and carry no connectivity.\n4) Seven LS outputs drive CMOS inputs with no pull-up: U7-2, U7-6, U7-12, \n   U26-4, U26-6, U26-10, U26-12. As-built; marginal high-level margin.\n5) HOST_TAPE_LOW (J2-24) is a DSI-specific use of that pin: +12 V normal, \n   −12 V when tape is low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
